# No code without a spec id

Valid ids live in `docs/spec/Dr.App.txt`: `FR-1.1.2`, `BR-02`, `§4.6.1`, or a named
non-functional requirement from §8.2. `scripts/trace.py` extracts them.

Tag every test with the id it covers. This is parsed, not decorative.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — nothing links this to the specification
test("creates a walk-in patient", async () => { ... });

// ✅ GOOD
/** @spec FR-2.2 — walk-in needs only mobile number and name, under 10 seconds. */
test("walk-in registration creates the patient and a per-practitioner token", async () => { ... });
```

Multiple ids on one test are fine: `@spec FR-1.5, BR-02`.

## If the spec does not say

Do not decide for it. In order:

1. Amend `docs/spec/Dr.App.txt`, adding a row to the §0.1 revision log stating what changed and why.
2. Regenerate: `python3 docs/spec/build-spec-html.py`.
3. Then write the test, then the code.

Never edit `docs/spec/Dr.App.Spec.html` by hand — it is generated output.

## Before claiming done

```bash
python3 scripts/trace.py          # regenerates docs/plan/TRACEABILITY.md, exits non-zero on gaps
./scripts/verify.sh               # everything
```

An id in the milestone currently in progress with no test covering it fails the build.
